<title>UK: UK monetary meeting begins.</title>
<headline>UK monetary meeting begins.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of England Governor Eddie George arrived at the UK Treasury building at around 0955 GMT on Wednesday, for his monthly monetary meeting with Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke.</p>
<p>The timing of the meeting means the Bank may signal any change in monetary policy in its money market operations around 1200 GMT. But traders will still watch early morning operations on Thursday for confirmation.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
